# RPC-node (validator-0) Canton persistence — STATUS: SHIPPED, IaC-CANONICAL.
#
# This file historically documented a manual `sed`-based patch of the live
# validator-0 wrapper + systemd unit to add `--config /config/node-config.toml`
# and `EnvironmentFile=/etc/tenzro/tenzro-node.env`. That approach was applied
# once on 2026-05-31 to bring the live RPC node up with Canton config without
# rebuilding the VM.
#
# It is now superseded:
#
# 1. The approach pivoted from `--config` (TOML overlay) to env-only.
#    `NodeConfig::load_from_file` is full-schema-only; partial overlay isn't
#    supported. `CantonConfig::from_env()` already covers the devnet profile
#    via `CANTON_DEVNET=true` + `CANTON_DEVNET_CLIENT_SECRET`, which is what
#    the wrapper now passes through. No TOML overlay file is needed; no
#    `--config` flag is set; `/etc/tenzro/node-config.toml` is not created.
#
# 2. The wrapper + units + fetch-canton-config script + `systemctl enable`
#    are all baked into `deploy/terraform/gce_validators/cloud-init.yaml`,
#    gated on `rpc_public == "true"`. Any future RPC-node rebuild from
#    terraform comes up with the full Canton stack on first boot — no manual
#    `sed` step required.
#
# 3. The standalone artifacts in this directory:
#
#      deploy/rpc-node/fetch-canton-config
#      deploy/rpc-node/tenzro-fetch-canton-config.service
#
#    are kept as exact copies of what cloud-init writes, in case the
#    validator-0 VM needs to be re-bootstrapped manually (e.g. before a full
#    terraform-driven rebuild). They are NOT the canonical source — cloud-init
#    is. If you edit one, edit both.
#
# The live state on validator-0 as of 2026-05-31:
#
#   - /var/lib/tenzro-bin/fetch-canton-config         (mode 0755 root)
#   - /etc/systemd/system/tenzro-fetch-canton-config.service
#   - /etc/tenzro/tenzro-node.env                     (mode 0600 root,
#                                                       TENZRO_ADMIN_TOKEN +
#                                                       CANTON_DEVNET_CLIENT_SECRET)
#   - /var/lib/tenzro-bin/tenzro-run                  (passes -e TENZRO_ADMIN_TOKEN
#                                                       -e CANTON_DEVNET=true
#                                                       -e CANTON_DEVNET_CLIENT_SECRET)
#   - /etc/systemd/system/tenzro-node.service         (EnvironmentFile +
#                                                       Requires=tenzro-fetch-canton-config)
#
# Verification (smoke tests passed against rpc.tenzro.network on 2026-05-31):
#
#   curl -s https://rpc.tenzro.network -X POST -H 'content-type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tenzro_listCantonDomains","params":[]}'
#   → -32004 "missing X-Tenzro-Api-Key header (required scope: canton)"
#     (admin gate passes, scope gate enforces — proves env loaded)
#
#   With X-Tenzro-Admin-Token, tenzro_createApiKey mints a scoped tnz_... key.
#   With X-Tenzro-Api-Key set to that key, tenzro_listCantonDomains returns
#   the live `canton-global-domain` synchronizer.
#
# Rotation: update Secret Manager → `systemctl restart tenzro-fetch-canton-config`
# → `docker stop tenzro-node` (systemd respawns with the new env). No rebuild.
